{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "mulesoft-test-collection",
		"name": "MuleSoft TEST Environment - Log Access",
		"description": "MuleSoft Anypoint Platform API collection for TEST environment (EU region).\n\n## Setup Instructions:\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Import the MuleSoft-TEST-Environment.json environment file\n3. Set the following environment variables:\n   - `mulesoft_client_id`: Your Connected App Client ID\n   - `mulesoft_client_secret`: Your Connected App Client Secret\n   - `mulesoft_base_url`: https://eu1.anypoint.mulesoft.com (EU region)\n   - `mulesoft_api_base_url`: https://eu1.anypoint.mulesoft.com/armui/api/v2\n   - `mulesoft_organization_id`: Your organization ID (REQUIRED)\n   - `mulesoft_environment_id`: TEST environment ID (REQUIRED)\n\n## Authentication:\nThis collection uses OAuth2 Client Credentials flow.\n1. Run the 'Get Access Token' request first\n2. The token will be automatically saved to `mulesoft_access_token` variable\n3. All subsequent requests use Bearer token authentication\n\n## Applications:\n- PAPI: sf-accounts-papi-qa\n- SAPI: accl-dataverse-sys-api-qa\n\n## Note:\nNo credentials are stored in this collection. All sensitive data should be stored in Postman environment variables.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{
				"key": "token",
				"value": "{{mulesoft_access_token}}",
				"type": "string"
			}
		]
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "base_url",
			"value": "{{mulesoft_base_url}}",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "api_base_url",
			"value": "{{mulesoft_api_base_url}}",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Authentication",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Access Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.environment.set('mulesoft_access_token', jsonData.access_token);",
									"    pm.environment.set('mulesoft_token_expires_in', jsonData.expires_in);",
									"    console.log('Access token saved to environment variable');",
									"    console.log('Token expires in: ' + jsonData.expires_in + ' seconds');",
									"} else {",
									"    console.log('Authentication failed');",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{
									"key": "client_id",
									"value": "{{mulesoft_client_id}}",
									"type": "text"
								},
								{
									"key": "client_secret",
									"value": "{{mulesoft_client_secret}}",
									"type": "text"
								},
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "client_credentials",
									"type": "text"
								}
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/accounts/api/v2/oauth2/token",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"accounts",
								"api",
								"v2",
								"oauth2",
								"token"
							]
						},
						"description": "Authenticates with MuleSoft Anypoint Platform using OAuth2 Client Credentials flow.\n\n**Required Variables:**\n- `mulesoft_client_id`: Connected App Client ID\n- `mulesoft_client_secret`: Connected App Client Secret\n\n**Response:**\n- `access_token`: Bearer token for API requests\n- `expires_in`: Token expiration time in seconds\n\n**Note:** The access token is automatically saved to the environment variable `mulesoft_access_token`."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get My Organization Info",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{mulesoft_access_token}}",
								"type": "text"
							},
							{
								"key": "Accept",
								"value": "application/json",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/accounts/api/me",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"accounts",
								"api",
								"me"
							]
						},
						"description": "Gets information about the authenticated user and organization.\n\n**Use this to find:**\n- Organization ID\n- User information\n- Organization details\n\n**Response includes:**\n- `organization.id`: Your Organization ID\n- `organization.name`: Organization name\n- User details\n\n**After running:**\n1. Look for `organization.id` in the response\n2. Copy it to `mulesoft_organization_id` environment variable"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "List Environments",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{mulesoft_access_token}}",
								"type": "text"
							},
							{
								"key": "Accept",
								"value": "application/json",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/accounts/api/organizations/{{mulesoft_organization_id}}/environments",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"accounts",
								"api",
								"organizations",
								"{{mulesoft_organization_id}}",
								"environments"
							]
						},
						"description": "Lists all environments in your organization.\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- Must have `mulesoft_organization_id` set first (use 'Get My Organization Info')\n\n**Use this to find:**\n- Environment ID for TEST environment\n\n**Response includes:**\n- Array of environments with:\n  - `id`: Environment ID\n  - `name`: Environment name (e.g., \"TEST\")\n  - `type`: Environment type\n\n**After running:**\n1. Find the environment with `name: \"TEST\"`\n2. Copy its `id` to `mulesoft_environment_id` environment variable"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		},
